00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.550 align:start position:0%
bioinformatics is the intersection of  informatics or the science of processing  data for storage and retrieval and  biology the study of living organisms  this field developed tremendously in the  last several decades transforming life  sciences enabling biotechnology and  empowering biomedical research  as a result came many new discoveries  that include new treatments for  different diseases diagnostic assays  design strategies for experimentation  and innovation in biotechnology as a  result there is a growing interest among  biologists and clinicians for data  including new types of data generation  computational methods of analysis as  well as approaches to find patterns that  can explain biological phenomena  a lot of breakthroughs in bioinformatics  are a result of high throughput  technologies like next-generation  sequencing that generate billions of  data points on genes proteins and other  molecules which characterize biological  systems  these data are compiled into  repositories that can be systematically  studied to understand and establish  trends for many applications one such  repository is maintained by the national  center of biotechnology information  which has a collection of peer-reviewed  articles biological data sets and  projects on various topics  the introduction to bioinformatics  program will introduce you to these  important terms and topics as a result  of completing the course you will see  the applications of next generation  sequencing biostatistical methods of  analysis and computational tools that  are used to process and mine big data  the training program combines biology  and data analysis concepts leveraging  the omics logic portal  there you will find a collection of  training modules that will help you get  started the program is designed to point  you to the relevant resources and  complete them over the course of the  semester  these resources will introduce  bioinformatics applications in  healthcare biomedical research  biotechnology and agriculture  provide you with a concise overview of  various biological concepts that you  need to know to understand omix data  introduce you to big data analysis using  several example data sets and expose you  to coding in r and python that are used  to analyze biological data  these are just several examples that  will lead into more in-depth review of  key omix technologies and analysis  methods  after this overview you will be able to  see how next-generation sequencing data  and bioinformatics are used in various  research areas like oncology infectious  diseases neuroscience and agriculture  you will also be introduced to the t  vitamin for platform for big data  analysis where you can run analysis of  large data without any technical  expertise  avoiding the challenges of piecing  together complex analytical pipelines  that typically bioinformaticians do  to see the full schedule we welcome you  to explore this page and start with your  journey into bioinformatics
 

